    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 🕉️ Gita Oracle — Day 4: HTTP & Credentials Deep Dive\n\nOne webhook, **six ways** to reach the same Groq model. Same question in, same response shape out — only the auth mechanism and prompt-building method change per branch. Study them side by side.\n\n| # | `method` value | What it teaches |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `agent` | n8n AI Agent — fully managed, no manual HTTP |\n| 2 | `predefined` | Dedicated `groqApi` credential type |\n| 3 | `header_auth` | Generic **Header Auth** — you type the header name |\n| 4 | `bearer_auth` | Generic **Bearer Auth** — built-in, no header typing |\n| 5 | `header_auth_persona` | Hidden key + custom system prompt |\n| 6 | `code_prompt` | Prompt built in a **Code node**, not inline |\n| 7 | `static_header` | ⚠️ Key typed directly into the header — no credential, anti-pattern |\n\n**Payload in:** `{ question, method, ts }`\n**Response out:** `{ reply, method }` or `{ error, validMethods }`",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 620,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "b5323087-a7e5-4660-be45-c00f75624eda",
      "name": "📖 Project Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1872,
        928
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 🔐 Before You Run This\n\n- [ ] `groqApi` credential → **Groq Chat Model** + **Groq via Predefined Credential**\n- [ ] **Header Auth** credential (`Authorization: Bearer <key>`) → Header Auth, Persona, and Code Prompt branches\n- [ ] **Bearer Auth** credential (raw token, *no* \"Bearer \" prefix — n8n adds it) → Bearer Auth branch\n- [ ] Activate workflow → copy the **production** webhook URL\n- [ ] Test all 6 branches with `mock-test-payloads.json`\n\n⚠️ **Never commit real API keys into this workflow's exported JSON.** That's the whole point of today's lesson — every credential above lives in n8n's vault, not in this file.",
        "height": 380,
        "width": 460,
        "color": 6
      },
